.TH PROLEWATCH-CONFIG 5 "September 2026" "Prolewatch" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
prolewatch-config \- Prolewatch policy and provider configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/prolewatch/config.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
The configuration is a YAML mapping. Prolewatch validates the complete file
before using it. Unknown fields, invalid values, and unsafe combinations stop
the command.
.PP
Validate edits with:
.PP
.EX
prolewatch config-check
.EE
.PP
The installed file contains comments for every field and is the full reference
for the running version.
.SH TOP-LEVEL FIELDS
.TP
.B provider
Selects the AI backend:
.BR codex ,
.BR anthropic ,
or
.BR ollama .
The provider is inactive while review mode is deterministic-only.
.TP
.B providers
Contains backend-specific model, effort, timeout, context, reasoning, and
residency settings.
.TP
.B review
Controls deterministic-only or AI mode, AI phases, decision thresholds,
confidence, batching, and provider time limits. Deterministic inspection runs
at every gate.
.TP
.B limits
Bounds scan input, archives, selected text, findings, and scan duration.
Coverage that exceeds a required limit blocks approval.
.TP
.B build
Defines memory, CPU, task, runtime, workspace, output, and disk-reserve limits
for contained package code.
.TP
.B network
Defines interactive broker limits. Public HTTP and HTTPS destinations require
approval for the current build phase.
.TP
.B vendor
Sets semantic scan depth for vendored dependency trees. All bytes remain part
of content binding at every depth.
.TP
.B terminal
Selects branded or plain terminal output. It does not alter policy decisions.
.SH AI REVIEW
The default mode is
.BR deterministic-only .
When AI review is enabled, its findings supplement the deterministic scanner.
They cannot clear deterministic findings.
.PP
An Ollama configuration requires a current quality attestation. Create or renew
it with:
.PP
.EX
prolewatch doctor --probe-llm-quality
.EE
.PP
Codex and Anthropic provider checks use:
.PP
.EX
prolewatch doctor
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/prolewatch/config.yaml
Active configuration. It is installed as a pacman backup file, so package
upgrades preserve administrator edits.
.TP
.I /usr/share/prolewatch/default-config.yaml
Complete packaged default for comparison and recovery.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/prolewatch/docs/ai-review.md
Provider setup, local model measurements, and tuning guidance.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR prolewatch (1),
.BR yay (8),
.BR makepkg (8)
